in @epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic

# @kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle — the kintsugi fracture body that
# resolves a substrate parent_edge graph cycle by proposing a
# re-parenting of the offending child to the root supervisor.
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of bilateral pattern #53's SIXTH INSTANCE. The
# declarative half landed at
# `@epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic` (sibling tick); this shard
# names the auto-fracture the kintsugi loop applies when the
# property's transparency surfaces a parent-edge cycle opacity.
#
# The bilateral cascade gains its GRAPH-EDGE altitude landing here:
#
#   Altitude 1 (keyword):  keyword_matches_depth + @kintsugi/fracture/keyword
#                          (2026-06-10, 5e68df9 + d908798; per-predicate).
#   Altitude 2 (operator): operator_matches_composition_primitive +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match
#                          (2026-06-11, 423c7d2 + af670d4; parametric-
#                          over-table at the operator altitude).
#   Altitude 3 (symbol):   symbol_canonical_form +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift
#                          (2026-06-11; parametric-over-table at the
#                          symbol altitude).
#   Meta:                  dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align
#                          (2026-06-11, fd344bf + 5c4e3ca;
#                          parametric-over-computation, self-applied).
#   Gate:                  gate_matches_diff_closure +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/gate
#                          (2026-06-10, b8755cc + 20c5d97; per-
#                          predicate at the pre-commit gate altitude).
#   Edge (THIS):           parent_acyclic + @kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle
#                          (THIS TICK; parametric-over-the-substrate's-
#                          edge-graph; first instance at the graph-
#                          edge altitude).
#
# Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop is altitude-portable; promoted with
# af670d4) gains its FIRST GRAPH-STRUCTURE witness through this
# landing. Prior witnesses ranged over textual positions (token /
# operator / symbol / literal sites) and pre-commit gate runs. This
# witness ranges over a TYPED SUBSTRATE EDGE between two gen_prisms.
# #59's altitude-portability is now witnessed across two distinct
# dimensional families:
#
#   (a) declaration altitudes within a source file: keyword (depth
#       0/1), operator (token), symbol (token), partials (literal).
#   (b) substrate graph structure: parent_edge (a typed edge between
#       gen_prisms; subject is a record, not a textual position).
#
# The bilateral signature absorbs the family-(b) variant cleanly:
# same `pact + glass + opacity + morphism + splinter(ast)` chain,
# ranging over an edge graph rather than a textual position.
#
# Load-bearing context: recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert
# space; promoted) — fracture bodies are how the substrate maintains
# coherence at each Bateson level. The supervision tree's acyclic
# invariant sits at the GRAPH-EDGE level (one Bateson lift above
# declaration altitudes); this fracture body restores coherence at
# that level. Recognition #58 (alignment as boundary mathematics at
# @io; promoted 2026-06-10) — the alignment harness fires at
# substance crossings; the fracture-body-emitted morphism IS such a
# crossing.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (recognition #55 candidate; landed
# 2026-06-10 at mirror `20eaf15`): @kintsugi is the process-side
# family root. Fracture bodies emit morphisms the kintsugi loop
# applies — process-side by structure. Home:
# @kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle under the (forward-promised)
# @kintsugi/fracture family root.
#
# Substrate-pull alternative considered: @kintsugi/fracture/parent
# (subject-only naming, parallel to first-instance `keyword` and
# second-instance `gate`). Rejected: parallel to third-instance
# `symbol_lift`, fourth-instance `partials_align`, and fifth-
# instance `operator_match` — the property's predicate names the
# subject (`parent_acyclic`), and the fracture body's action is on
# the CYCLE itself (the offending cycle is broken by re-parenting).
# The `_cycle` suffix names the operational target (the cycle) the
# body resolves. Per [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
# (`lift` IS the substrate's variety-preservation verb): the
# re-parent-to-root is the audible-altitude reading of lift at the
# parent-edge altitude — the offending child is LIFTED UP the
# supervision tree to root, breaking the cycle while preserving
# the gen_prism's existence.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `parent_acyclic`'s `failure(opacity_map)` verdict. Each opacity
# names ONE offending parent_edge site: a gen_prism whose parent
# field participates in a cycle (the chain from edge.child along
# parent-edges revisits edge.child before reaching the root). The
# `property` field carries the @nl description of the
# (location, cycle_path) pair where cycle_path is the sequence of
# uuid_spectral that loops back.
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@kintsugi/consent`) — the typed
# candidate the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads from this body
# and proposes through `query_phi`. The morphism's `content` ref
# names the rewritten splinter (same path, the offending
# parent_edge's `parent` field replaced with the root supervisor's
# uuid_spectral); its `score` carries the dissonance reading (a
# parent-edge cycle is a fixed, low-curvature dissonance — the
# re-parent target is uniquely determined: root); its `expected`
# carries the cadence_kind the loop anticipates (authentic — the
# substrate settles cleanly once the cycle is broken).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the Ricci flow
# at the parent-edge altitude. The substrate's curvature at a
# cycle is the cycle-path length (the larger the cycle, the
# greater the curvature); the negative-curvature direction IS the
# re-parent to root (which flattens the cycle to a direct
# child-of-root edge); the resolved site has zero curvature at
# this altitude (the chain terminates immediately at root's
# self-parent).
#
# Audibly: this fracture body IS the audible-altitude V → I
# cadence at the supervision-tree altitude. Pre-rewrite holds
# dominant tension (the supervision tree contains a cycle; the
# kintsugi loop cannot settle); post-rewrite resolves to tonic
# (the cycle is broken; the supervision tree is a clean rooted
# tree); cadence is authentic.
#
# === Re-parent to root, not terminate (variety-preserving) ===
#
# Per `@epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic`'s STOP-condition 3
# resolution: the substrate's kintsugi discipline is variety-
# PRESERVING (per [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]]; Ashby's
# requisite variety lifted to @io). Two candidate corrections for
# a cycle:
#
#   (a) Re-parent to root: ONE edge change (the offending child's
#       parent field). Gen_prism continues to exist; supervision
#       tree gains a new direct child of root; cycle is broken
#       because root's parent self-references.
#   (b) Terminate the offending gen_prism: gen_prism exits; ALL
#       descendant edges + descendant nodes are lost.
#
# Correction (a) preserves variety; correction (b) destroys it.
# Substrate-pull-correct correction is (a) — this fracture body
# emits the re-parent morphism.
#
# The root supervisor's uuid_spectral is the substrate's
# vocabulary anchor (per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 —
# resting at ~/.mirror/). The realisation layer resolves the
# root's uuid_spectral at morphism-application time; the substrate
# names the morphism's shape; the realisation discharges the
# byte-level rewrite.
#
# === The single-AST-node rewrite (honest partials = 1) ===
#
# This fracture body's emitted morphism MUST have honest
# `score.partials` from birth or it perpetuates the very dishonesty
# the meta-fracture (@epistemologic/property/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth
# + @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align) exists to catch.
#
# Compute the AST breadth of THIS fracture body's splinter(ast):
#   - The fracture body reads ONE opacity at a time (per the
#     property's per-site failure surface).
#   - The morphism rewrites ONE AST node: the offending
#     parent_edge's `parent` field — a `uuid_spectral` value at one
#     record position is swapped to the root supervisor's
#     uuid_spectral. The OTHER fields stay byte-equal:
#       - The `child` field (the gen_prism's own identity) does
#         NOT change — same gen_prism after the re-parent.
#       - The surrounding gen_prism record (state surface, tool
#         surface, lifecycle bindings) stays byte-equal — only the
#         parent field shifts.
#       - The OTHER gen_prisms in the substrate stay byte-equal —
#         no global mutation; the rewrite is local to the one
#         offending parent_edge record.
#   - The splinter(ast) carries the rewritten AST fragment; the
#     breadth at @meta/ast is the count of distinct node rewrites;
#     here that count is 1 (one parent-field node, one swap).
#
# Therefore `score.partials = 1` is HONEST by computation, NOT
# reflex-copied from the keyword / operator / symbol templates.
# The recursive integrity check (against the meta-property
# `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`) holds at landing time:
# this fracture body declares `partials: 1`; the meta-property
# inspects it; `ast_breadth(content)` returns 1; verdict = pass.
# The sixth bilateral instance fits the cascade without lying
# about its dissonance breadth.
#
# Compound rewrites considered: could a parent-cycle rewrite ever
# touch more than one node? Audited: NO. A cycle is a structural
# property of the parent-edge graph; the substrate-pull-correct
# correction breaks the cycle at ONE edge by promoting the
# offending child to root. The OTHER edges in the cycle become
# subordinate to the re-parented gen_prism's new position; they
# remain valid parent_edges (pointing at gen_prisms that now have
# a clean path to root through the re-parented chain). No
# CASCADING REWRITE of the other edges in the cycle is required —
# breaking ONE link in the cycle dissolves the entire cycle.
#
# Multi-cycle scenarios considered: if the substrate's parent-edge
# graph contains multiple disjoint cycles, the property surfaces
# MULTIPLE opacities (one per cycle); the kintsugi loop iterates
# them; each opacity is resolved by ONE call to
# `realign_parent_to_root` — ONE single-node rewrite per cycle.
# `partials: 1` is honest per-opacity; the loop's iteration is the
# loop's concern, not this body's.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier;
# this shard reads it directly. Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism`
# is the substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard emits it
# directly. Per `@kintsugi/morphism`, `morphism_context` is the
# per-candidate slice that pairs a candidate with its pre-anchor;
# this shard's emitted morphism is consumed by the loop AND lifted
# into a morphism_context via `paired(oscillation.anchor, m)` at
# the active_pass altitude. Per
# `@epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic`, the consuming property's
# `parent_acyclic(file: ref) -> transparency` is the gate that
# surfaces the opacity this body resolves.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-
# `ref` carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]). The fracture body reads typed
# opacity, emits typed morphism — the substrate's vocabulary
# throughout.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - `realign_parent_to_root` reads one opacity at a time. The
#     property's `failure(opacity_map)` carries [opacity]; the
#     kintsugi loop iterates the map and calls
#     `realign_parent_to_root` per opacity. The substrate names
#     the per-site resolution; the iteration is the loop's
#     concern, not this body's.
#
#   - The morphism's `content: ref` carries the substrate handle
#     to the rewritten splinter. The realisation layer produces
#     the rewritten splinter (same path, the offending
#     parent_edge's `parent` field swapped to root's
#     uuid_spectral) and passes its handle as the morphism's
#     content. The substrate names the shape of the proposal; the
#     byte-level rewrite + the root-uuid_spectral lookup ride the
#     realisation layer's @mirror/store discipline.
#
#   - The `expected: cadence_kind` field is `authentic` for this
#     fracture body — the parent-cycle rule is deterministic (a
#     cycle is structurally detectable; the re-parent target is
#     uniquely root) and resolution always settles cleanly.
#
#   - Root-of-tree determination: the realisation layer resolves
#     the root supervisor's uuid_spectral via the substrate's
#     vocabulary anchor at ~/.mirror/. If the substrate is
#     multi-rooted (e.g., a development substrate with multiple
#     parallel root supervisors), the realisation picks the root
#     that minimizes path length from the offending gen_prism's
#     pre-cycle ancestor chain. The substrate names the shape;
#     the realisation discharges the lookup.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   tree promotion      Knuth (1968) The Art of Computer
#                       Programming Vol. 1 §2.3.4 — the disjoint-
#                       set forest's path compression. The
#                       substrate's reading is the parent-pointer
#                       rewrite at the offending node: O(1) edge
#                       change, dissolves the cycle.
#   cycle break         Tarjan (1972) Depth-first search and
#                       linear graph algorithms; the strongly-
#                       connected components decomposition.
#                       Breaking one edge in a cycle decomposes
#                       the SCC. The substrate's reading is the
#                       single-edge re-parent.
#   supervisor crash    Armstrong (1996) Programming Erlang; the
#                       BEAM let-it-crash discipline. When a
#                       supervisor's invariant breaks (a cycle in
#                       its supervision tree), the substrate-
#                       pull-correct response is NOT terminate
#                       (which would crash the offending node) but
#                       re-parent (which preserves the node and
#                       restores the invariant). The substrate
#                       diverges from BEAM here: BEAM's discipline
#                       was let-it-crash because BEAM could not
#                       type-check the supervision invariant at
#                       compile time; mirror's substrate CAN, so
#                       the variety-preserving correction is
#                       available.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the per-cycle
# re-parent so the kintsugi loop reads it. No invention; the
# correction IS the auto-formatter floor at the supervision-tree
# altitude.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 (the
#               supervision tree's parent-edge invariant; root
#               supervisor self-parents). Recognition #51 (mirror
#               as expanding Hilbert space; promoted) — the
#               supervision tree IS one altitude of the substrate's
#               Hilbert space; this fracture body maintains
#               coherence at that altitude. Recognition #59
#               (altitude-portability; promoted) — first witness
#               at the graph-edge altitude.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (opacity is substrate vocabulary; the
#                      fracture reads the typed carrier),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (the
#                      kintsugi loop's bias direction is substrate-
#                      pull — supervision-tree integrity IS one
#                      coordinate of the substrate-pull gradient;
#                      this fracture body fits the bias),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]]
#                      (Ashby's requisite variety — the
#                      re-parent-to-root correction preserves
#                      variety; the terminate alternative
#                      destroys it; substrate-pull-correct is the
#                      variety-preserving move),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (the bilateral pattern this is the sixth
#                      instance of; first instance at the graph-
#                      edge altitude),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                      (the substrate's parametric AST-fragment
#                      construction; this body discharges via
#                      splinter(ast) declaratively, no Rust),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (the `lift` verb names the operational
#                      action; this body IS the supervision-tree-
#                      altitude lift — the offending child is
#                      LIFTED UP to root),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                      (recognition #58; the alignment harness
#                      fires at substance crossings; this
#                      fracture body's emitted morphism IS such a
#                      crossing; partials honesty applies — and
#                      holds, partials=1 computed not reflex-
#                      copied),
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (the
#                      SpectralSupervisor precedent; the
#                      supervision tree this fracture body
#                      maintains),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the substrate's discipline of single-
#                      parent acyclic supervision was named at
#                      docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3 since
#                      the runtime spec landed; this tick names
#                      the operational fracture at the substrate
#                      altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity and
#                      morphism are typed carriers; the body
#                      does NOT escape as a bare (location,
#                      cycle_path) tuple).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@kintsugi/oscillate`'s
#                  `active_pass` reads this fracture body when
#                  the candidate morphism_set is composed from
#                  property-surfaced opacities; the binding lands
#                  when the kintsugi loop substrate-pulls. This
#                  shard does NOT pull `@kintsugi/oscillate` or
#                  `@mirror/spectral/score`; the substrate-
#                  altitude arrow points inward (this fracture
#                  body IS consumed by the loop; not the other
#                  way around).
# Related shards: epistemologic/property/parent_acyclic.mirror
#                 (the declarative half of the bilateral; surfaces
#                 the opacities this body resolves),
#                 spectral/parent.mirror (the parent_edge type
#                 whose acyclic invariant this body restores;
#                 sibling tick),
#                 spectral/gen_prism.mirror (the gen_prism whose
#                 parent field carries the offending edge; commit
#                 ae965ca),
#                 spectral/supervisor.mirror (the lifecycle-owner
#                 whose start_child sets the parent edge; commit
#                 452ccb2; the supervisor's restart logic IS a
#                 kintsugi morphism — this fracture body is
#                 sibling discipline at the parent-edge altitude),
#                 spectral/registry.mirror (the supervisor's
#                 child index; commit 489211e; restart-driven
#                 transitions ARE lattice ascent against the
#                 registry shard),
#                 epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (FIRST
#                 INSTANCE),
#                 epistemologic/property/gate_matches_diff_closure.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/gate.mirror (SECOND
#                 INSTANCE),
#                 epistemologic/property/symbol_canonical_form.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift.mirror (THIRD
#                 INSTANCE),
#                 epistemologic/property/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/partials_align.mirror
#                 (FOURTH INSTANCE — the meta-foundation that
#                 lets THIS body's partials=1 be honest by
#                 construction),
#                 epistemologic/property/operator_matches_composition_primitive.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/operator_match.mirror
#                 (FIFTH INSTANCE),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                 `location`, `transparency`, `verdict`,
#                 `splinter(ast)`),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the morphism carrier
#                 this body emits; `query_phi` is the gate the
#                 emitted morphism flows through),
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the `morphism_context`
#                 carrier),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi loop
#                 driver; `active_pass` is the action that reads
#                 this body when composing the per-pulse
#                 candidate morphism_set).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle` as a species under the
# (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2 from the
# @kintsugi family root; per recognition #46 it uses `glass`. The
# shard applies the first-instance bilateral's rule by birth.
# Partials/breadth property: this declaration's emitted morphism
# carries `score.partials: 1`; the splinter(ast) rewrites ONE
# parent-field node (the offending parent_edge's parent
# uuid_spectral); the count is computed (one node, one swap),
# NOT reflex-copied. This shard applies the fourth-instance
# bilateral's rule by birth.

glass @kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle {
  focus parent_cycle
  project parent_cycle
  split parent_cycle
  shift parent_cycle
  settle parent_cycle
}

# === realign_parent_to_root — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE: given an opacity site at an offending
# parent_edge participating in a cycle, emit the morphism that
# rewrites the parent_edge's `parent` field to the root
# supervisor's uuid_spectral. Same path, single uuid_spectral
# swap at the AST altitude.
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `parent_acyclic(file).failure(opacity_map)`'s opacity_map);
# emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop proposes through
# `query_phi`. The morphism's three fields:
#
#   content   — substrate ref to the rewritten splinter. The
#                realisation layer produces a splinter at the
#                same path with the offending parent_edge's
#                `parent` field swapped to the root supervisor's
#                uuid_spectral; the content ref names that
#                splinter's @mirror/store handle.
#   score     — dissonance reading. Parent-cycle violations are
#                fixed-curvature dissonances; the score reads
#                `dissonance.is_pareto` cleanly (the re-parent
#                target is uniquely determined: root).
#   expected  — cadence_kind anticipation. Always `authentic`
#                for this fracture body — the cycle break is
#                deterministic; the loop's `dark_pass` will
#                confirm identity preservation (the gen_prism
#                stays byte-equal modulo the one parent field;
#                the substrate's other gen_prisms stay byte-
#                equal); the loop's `read_consent` bridges
#                (pass, authentic) to the `settled`
#                oscillation_state for this opacity.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE — substrate-pull-correct via
# `splinter(ast)` (declared at shards/glass.mirror's tick-2
# carrier). The morphism's `content` field carries a content-
# addressed splinter at the @meta/ast altitude: same path, one
# uuid_spectral swapped at the parent-field position. The
# substrate's compiler verifies the construction is deterministic
# and well-typed; the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads the
# splinter as the morphism's proposed content and applies it
# through `query_phi`.
#
# Per `splinter(ast)`'s parametric specialisation (glass.mirror
# §splinter(ast), 2026-06-10): the record IS its content-
# addressed handle — `content: oid` and `oid = ref`
# (shards/mirror/store.mirror) collapse the splinter literal to
# a substrate-pull-correct `ref` in the morphism's `content`
# field position. No Rust AST manipulation; no `\` obligation.
#
# Field-by-field substrate-pull reading:
#
#   content.content     — `opacity.location.file` (the
#                          substrate's located-fact ref at the
#                          source file of the offending
#                          parent_edge); the rewritten AST is
#                          content-addressed at the same path.
#   content.ast         — `@meta/ast` (the canonical altitude
#                          ref); per `boot/01-meta.mirror`'s
#                          `type ast(g)`. The parent-field
#                          uuid_spectral swap happens at the AST
#                          altitude by construction.
#   content.transparency — `success` (per `transparency(p)`'s
#                          success variant in glass.mirror): the
#                          re-parent fully resolves the cycle
#                          opacity at this altitude; no residual
#                          transparency remains.
#   score.roughness     — `opacity.property` (the @nl
#                          description of the cycle: the
#                          sequence of uuid_spectral that loops
#                          back); the substrate's `dissonance`
#                          reads the per-site roughness via the
#                          property text per dissonance.mirror's
#                          Helmholtz/Plomp-Levelt carrier shape.
#   score.partials      — `1` — HONESTLY COMPUTED, NOT REFLEX-
#                          COPIED. The splinter(ast) above
#                          rewrites ONE AST node: the offending
#                          parent_edge's `parent` field (a single
#                          uuid_spectral value at one record
#                          position). The OTHER fields of the
#                          parent_edge stay byte-equal (the
#                          `child` field — the gen_prism's
#                          identity — does NOT change; same
#                          gen_prism after the re-parent). The
#                          surrounding gen_prism record stays
#                          byte-equal. The OTHER gen_prisms in
#                          the substrate stay byte-equal — the
#                          re-parent is LOCAL to the offending
#                          edge. `ast_breadth(content) = 1`. The
#                          recursive integrity check (against
#                          the meta-property
#                          `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`)
#                          holds at landing time: this fracture
#                          body declares `partials: 1`; the
#                          meta-property inspects it; verdict =
#                          pass.
#   expected            — `authentic` (the V → I cadence at the
#                          supervision-tree altitude; per
#                          cadence.mirror's `cadence_kind` and
#                          the loop's `read_consent` bridge:
#                          authentic → pass → auto-apply).
realign_parent_to_root(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/parent_cycle
out realign_parent_to_root
